The fence goes into the entry past the last the image may use,
the first the core hardwires on RP2350, which takes no write,
so the hardwired entries grant user mode every right over the peripherals
to a process that holds no frame for them.

Caught-by: fuzz-rp2350
Report: PMP CSRs grant rights the slots do not

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -17,8 +17,8 @@
 void process_fence(void)
 {
     if (pmp_entry_end > pmp_entry_count) {
-        pmp_entry_count--;
         pmp_set(pmp_entry_count, PMP_NAPOT_ALL, PMP_A_NAPOT);
+        pmp_entry_count--;
     }
 }
 
